        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://facts.net/world/cities/10-facts-about-linton-indiana/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around coal mining, earning a reputation as a coal mining city southeast of Terre Haute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linton%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1908 a Carnegie library was built; the historic Margaret Cooper Public Library now houses Phil Harris and Alice Faye memorabilia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linton%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "General Electric opened a factory in 1952 that employed hundreds until the mid‑1980s, but the building stayed empty until 2014 when GE tore it down.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linton%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Linton’s downtown features a giant shovel monument that nods to its mining heritage and draws curious visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://facts.net/world/cities/10-facts-about-linton-indiana/",
